DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     bbhhyyvvee is a hypervisor that runs guest operating systems inside a virtual
     machine.

     Parameters such as the number of virtual CPUs, amount of guest memory,
     and I/O connectivity can be specified with command-line parameters.

     If not using a boot ROM, the guest operating system must be loaded with
     bhyveload(8) or a similar boot loader before running bbhhyyvvee, otherwise, it
     is enough to run bbhhyyvvee with a boot ROM of choice.

     bbhhyyvvee runs until the guest operating system reboots or an unhandled hy‐
     pervisor exit is detected.

